From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:03:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] vdin: switch a channel's tap per frame past the channel count

A loopback stream needed a write-back channel for each tap, so two taps
on a one-channel SoC, or three on a two-channel one, were refused and
the client restarted the stream for every switch. The channel selects
share one register word, which one table can write per frame.
